   "Adopt clock/reset/HDL target contract; implement state-machine lowering and simulation; verify timing/reset invariants and reject illegal dynamic/runtime operations; emit traceable hardware artifact. DOM1 acceptance requires fixed synthesis-visible shapes, finite iteration and explicit CDC synchronizer/FIFO/handshake, proof or audit waiver; reject implicit widths/truncation, unsafe CDC, runtime-only constructs and nonfinite loops. Emit HDL, interface/clock/reset/timing records, source maps, testbench and simulation evidence. Exercise FIFO full/empty/reset/backpressure/data order plus counter and bus-peripheral fixtures. Dependencies: profile legality, HDL lowering, no-runtime and safety/proof consumers; target choice remains open ; P8 target conformance requires fixed-width shape/overflow checks, static unroll or structural conversion or rejection, explicit input-only nondeterminism, state-graph emission AND validation (initial/reset/transition/output/illegal-state behavior), clock/reset records (explicit uninitialized state allowed; unsafe power-on needs hardware audit), ports/protocols and CDC synchronizer/FIFO/handshake/proof or audited waiver. Reject runtime services and unmediated CDC. Capability targets must validate bounds/provenance/permissions/sealing/derivation, tags across register/memory/DMA/FIFO/bus/debug/port paths, declared compartment entry/return/shared-state authority and explicit temporal assumptions. Tag-destroying paths are marked and diagnosed unless source explicitly expects destruction; audited authority boundaries retain their conditions. A conforming target may declare no temporal revocation; stronger source requirements then reject or require separate proof. Emit source-mapped hardware IR/HDL, target/layout/tag/clock/reset/timing/port/compartment reports and positive/negative capability-target fixtures. ISA/product/fabrication selection remains unassessed For this target, the architecture owner records the concrete target/ABI, accepted artifact kind, named simulator/device evidence and required service set before implementation scope is claimed. Reject a scope claim missing any required selection or incompatible with the declared profile; no target or product is selected by this task. Target integration consumes the exact Lower/Emit artifact and explicit runtime or no-runtime manifest plus required standard-library adapters. Record actual simulation/execution and applicable layout, clock, interrupt, unsafe-island, grant and source-to-artifact provenance checks; reject forbidden services, missing adapters, unauditable authority or a record-only execution claim. These target gates do not require completion of the full Platform Product.",
   :label "Declared completion and remaining work",
   :id "hardware",
   :before
